UPDATE companies SET description='Barber Packaging Company was founded in 1989 in Bangor, Michigan, as a family-owned and operated business. The company began with a focus on building long-term partnerships through engineered packaging solutions.

The company provides a full-service approach to protective packaging, covering design and engineering using CAD technology, rapid prototyping, manufacturing, validation and testing, and program management. Its product range includes returnable packaging made from steel, wood, plastics, textiles, and foam; expendable packaging for export and retail; work-in-process material handling systems; and service/backup packaging. Manufacturing capabilities include CNC abrasive wire, CNC oscillating and tangential cutting, and automated assembly.

Barber serves a variety of industries that require protective packaging, though specific sectors are not listed publicly. Customers include OEMs and assembly plants needing intra-plant material handling, export shipping solutions, and custom protective packaging for product protection.

The company differentiates itself through "The Barber Way," a relationship-based philosophy emphasizing simple coordination, faster turnaround, cost savings, and single-source solutions. Its in-house design team and accredited lab partnerships enable quick iteration and compliance testing, while program management ensures projects stay on schedule and budget.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design & Engineering (CAD)", "Rapid Prototyping (form, fit, testing)", "Manufacturing (CNC abrasive wire, CNC oscillating/tangential, automated assembly)", "Validation & Testing (accredited labs, shake/drop testing)", "Program Management", "Returnable Packaging Design", "Expendable Packaging Design", "Work-in-Process (WIP) Material Handling Design", "Service/Backup Packaging Design", "Export Packaging Design"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Steel", "Wood", "Plastics", "Textiles", "Foam", "Corrugated", "Plastic Corrugated"], "equipment": ["CNC Abrasive Wire", "CNC Oscillating and Tangential", "Automated Assembly"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service approach from design through program management", "In-house CAD design and rapid prototyping with form, fit, and testing", "Manufacturing floor with CNC abrasive wire, oscillating/tangential cutting, and automated assembly", "Validation and testing via accredited labs and in-house shake/drop simulation", "Family-owned, relationship-driven partnerships spanning decades"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989, family-owned -> db (founded_year, description) and page ''/about''", "Headquarters Bangor, Michigan -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Full-service approach: design, prototyping, manufacturing, validation, program management -> page ''/'' and ''/services''", "Products: returnable, expendable, WIP, service/backup, export -> page ''/''", "Materials: steel, wood, plastics, textiles, foam, corrugated -> page ''/'' products list", "Equipment: CNC Abrasive Wire, CNC Oscillating and Tangential, Automated Assembly -> page ''/'' products array", "Industries served: various, not specified -> page ''/'' Industries Served section", "The Barber Way philosophy -> page ''/'' and ''/about''", "LinkedIn URL -> db (linkedin_url)", "In-house CAD design -> page ''/services''", "Rapid prototyping with form fit testing -> page ''/services''", "Validation with accredited labs -> page ''/services''", "Program management -> page ''/services''", "Family-owned since 1989 -> page ''/'' and db description"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From design concept and prototyping to production and program management, the Barber Team takes pride in delivering solutions to help your business.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/barber-packaging-company/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='barber-packaging-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bardot Plastics operates from a modern facility in Easton, Pennsylvania, where it has been manufacturing precision injection-molded parts since 1973. The company was founded by J. Lee Boucher and remains a third-generation family business, now led by his sons Chris, Jim, and Rick Boucher. What began as a vision for superior injection molding has grown into a full-service operation built on the principle of “making it right the first time.”

The shop specializes in large-tonnage molding, running presses up to 1,760 tons to produce large, complex components that many molders cannot accommodate. Its end-to-end capabilities cover design consultation, integrated tooling (single-cavity, multi-cavity, and family molds), insert molding, sonic welding, sub-assembly, and in-house packaging and fulfillment. A 120-ton central chilling unit and robotic part-removal systems support consistent quality across prototype and high-volume runs, working with both engineered and non-engineered resins.

Bardot serves a diverse industrial base including office furniture, lawn and garden, waste and recycling, industrial equipment, military, construction, agricultural, and commercial markets. Customers rely on the company for ergonomic workplace components, durable industrial parts, military-spec precision pieces, weather-resistant outdoor products, structural components, and agricultural parts built to withstand harsh environments.

The company differentiates itself through continuous technology investment — exemplified by the recent chilling unit installation — and a single-point-of-contact project management model. Its guiding principles of excellence, innovation, sustainability, and partnership reflect a heritage of delivering tight tolerances and dimensional stability regardless of part size or complexity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Large-tonnage injection molding (up to 1,760 tons)", "Integrated tooling design and construction (single-cavity, multi-cavity, family molds)", "Insert molding", "Post-molding assembly (sonic welding)", "Single-vendor sub-assembly", "In-house packaging and fulfillment", "Design for manufacturability consultation", "Tooling consultation and cost analysis", "Tooling validation and pre-production tuning", "Quality assurance and control (QA/QC)", "Robotics-assisted part removal", "Precision molding with tight tolerances", "High-volume production", "Prototyping and first-article inspection"], "industries": ["Office Furniture", "Lawn & Garden", "Waste & Recycling", "Industrial", "Military", "Construction", "Agricultural", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Engineered resins", "Non-engineered resins"], "equipment": ["1,760-ton injection molding presses", "120-ton central chilling unit", "Robotic part removal systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Large-tonnage molding capacity up to 1,760 tons for oversized parts", "Integrated tooling design and build (single-cavity, multi-cavity, family molds)", "Insert molding, sonic welding, and full sub-assembly under one roof", "In-house packaging and fulfillment with domestic and international shipping", "Third-generation family ownership with dedicated project managers"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1973 by J. Lee Boucher -> /about", "Third-generation family business led by Chris, Jim, and Rick Boucher -> /about", "Headquartered in Easton, Pennsylvania -> /, /about", "Large-tonnage injection molding up to 1,760 tons -> /, /capabilities", "120-ton central chilling unit installed -> /, /about, /capabilities", "Integrated tooling capabilities (single-cavity, multi-cavity, family molds) -> /capabilities", "Insert molding and post-molding assembly including sonic welding -> /capabilities", "Single-vendor assembly and in-house packaging & fulfillment -> /capabilities", "Industries served: Office Furniture, Lawn & Garden, Waste & Recycling, Industrial, Military, Construction, Agricultural, Commercial -> /", "Works with engineered and non-engineered resins -> /about", "Dedicated project managers as single point of contact -> /, /capabilities", "Quality mantra: ''making it right the first time'' -> /, /about, /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializing in large tonnage molding up to 1,760 tons. From initial design through final production, our state-of-the-art facility in Easton, PA delivers the precision, quality, and reliability your projects demand.", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bardot-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Barrington Wood Works LLC was founded in April 2018 in Lake Barrington, Illinois. The company entered the custom millwork industry with a focus on direct collaboration with clients, designers, and architects, producing shop drawings for each project.

It also offers semi‑custom cabinetry and pre‑installs assemblies to simplify final installation. Processes include hand scraping, machining, and faux finishes.

The firm serves both commercial and residential customers across the Greater Chicagoland area, including communities such as Arlington Heights, Barrington, Lake Forest, Naperville, and Winnetka. It works directly with designers and architects and supplies cabinetry from brands such as Crystal Cabinets, Fabuwood Cabinets, and Showplace Cabinetry.

