UPDATE companies SET description='Bayne Custom Woodworking operates from a 20-by-25-foot outbuilding in Mt. Juliet, Tennessee, just east of Nashville. The business took shape after Roger Bayne ended a decades-long career in information technology, stepping away from his office on March 12, 2021, to focus full-time on woodworking. Bayne, who first learned the craft out of necessity while raising a family on a warehouse salary, runs the shop with support from his wife, a graphic designer.

The shop produces custom furniture—dining tables, kitchen islands, cabinets, bookshelves, and live-edge pieces—along with smaller items such as cutting boards, chess sets, and Adirondack chairs. Each project begins with a SketchUp model so clients can review dimensions, joinery, and finish before any wood is cut. Lumber is hand-selected from Middle Tennessee mills (maple, oak, walnut, cherry, alder, poplar) and cedar from Grant Cedar Mill, then milled on a jointer and planer in the shop. Finishes include hand-wiped polyurethane and Tung oil for outdoor durability.

The clientele is primarily residential homeowners across Middle Tennessee seeking one-of-a-kind pieces or restoration of family heirlooms. Bayne also builds outdoor furniture designed for the region’s climate, using locally sourced cedar sealed with Tung oil. Projects range from a farm table with an integrated racetrack to a bunk bed for grandchildren, reflecting the shop’s willingness to tackle unconventional requests.

Bayne emphasizes that the shop does not manufacture in volume; every piece is built one at a time, with the owner making every measure and cut. The combination of 3D design transparency, local material sourcing, and a focus on preserving memories through restoration distinguishes the operation in a market dominated by mass-produced furniture.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and build", "Furniture restoration and renewal", "Live-edge furniture fabrication", "Outdoor furniture (Adirondack chairs, garden benches, planters)", "3D design (SketchUp)", "Lumber milling (jointer, planer)", "Finishing (hand-wiped polyurethane, Tung oil)", "Small wooden goods (cutting boards, chess boards, recipe stands)"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom woodworking", "Furniture restoration", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Maple", "Red Oak", "White Oak", "Walnut", "Cherry", "Alder", "Poplar", "Cedar (Tennessee Red Cedar)", "Reclaimed wood", "Hardwood"], "equipment": ["Craftsman table saw", "Band saw", "Disk sander (grinder converted)", "Jointer", "Planer", "SketchUp (3D design software)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Every project starts with a detailed 3D drawing in SketchUp", "Lumber hand-picked from local Tennessee mills and milled in-house", "One-of-a-kind pieces built one at a time by the owner", "Restoration and renewal of heirloom furniture", "Outdoor cedar products sealed with Tung oil for Tennessee climate"], "facts_used": ["Location: Mt. Juliet, Tennessee -> db", "Founder: Roger Bayne -> /, /about", "Transition to full-time woodworking in 2021 -> /about", "Shop size: 20'' x 25'' outbuilding -> /about", "Processes: custom furniture, restoration, live-edge, outdoor cedar -> /, /services", "3D design in SketchUp -> /, /services", "Local lumber sourcing: Middle Tennessee mills, Grant Cedar Mill -> /, /services", "Wood species: maple, red oak, white oak, walnut, cherry, alder, po