UPDATE companies SET description='Beacon Metal Fabricators was founded in 1987 in Cleveland, Ohio, with a straightforward mission: do solid work, treat people right, and make things that last. The shop began as a small operation focused on custom metal fabrication and has since grown into a full-service partner for short-run and specialty projects.

The company provides a broad range of in-house metalworking capabilities, including laser cutting, CNC bending, TIG/MIG/Stick welding, rolling and forming, wire fabrication, resistance and spot welding, fastener insertion, custom tool building, and finishing services such as grinding, polishing, and coating. It specializes in prototype and low-volume production — typically dozens to a few thousand parts — and handles projects from custom electrical cabinets and lighting restoration components to transportation prototypes and aftermarket automotive parts.

Beacon serves a diverse client base across transportation and prototyping, electrical contractors needing custom enclosures, architectural and lighting restoration for historic buildings, public art and structural fabrication, and general industrial and commercial accounts. Notable projects include retrofit parts for century-old bronze fixtures in churches and municipal buildings, and custom-sized electrical cabinets for hospitals and schools where standard products do not fit.

The shop differentiates itself by taking on the "odd jobs" that larger manufacturers decline — short runs, tricky fits, and one-off builds — emphasizing flexibility and craftsmanship over volume. It manufactures to UL, NSF, and NAEF standards as required, and maintains a nimble, problem-solving approach that allows quick pivots and tight deadlines without formal ISO or ITAR certifications.', certifications=ARRAY['UL standards','NSF standards','NAEF standards']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser Cutting", "CNC Bending", "TIG Welding", "MIG Welding", "Stick Welding", "Rolling & Forming", "Wire Fabrication", "Resistance Welding", "Spot Welding", "Fastener Insertion", "Machine & Tool Building", "Finishing (Grinding, Polishing, Coatings)", "Custom Electrical Cabinet Fabrication", "Lighting Restoration Component Fabrication", "Prototype & Small-Volume Fabrication", "Sheet Metal Fabrication", "Steel Fabrication", "Assembly"], "industries": ["Transportation & Prototyping", "Automotive (Aftermarket)", "Electrical Contractors", "Architectural & Lighting Restoration", "Public Art & Structural Fabrication", "Industrial & Commercial Clients", "Healthcare (Hospitals)", "Education (Schools)", "Municipal"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless Steel", "Carbon Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype and short-run production (dozens to thousands of parts)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in short-run and prototype fabrication that larger shops decline", "Broad in-house capabilities: laser cutting, CNC bending, welding (TIG/MIG/Stick), rolling, wire fabrication, fastener insertion, finishing", "Flexible, nimble operation able to pivot quickly and meet hard deadlines", "Manufactures to UL, NSF, and NAEF standards as required", "Takes on custom one-offs, odd jobs, and specialty repairs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1987 -> db, /, /about", "Headquarters in Cleveland, Ohio -> db, /, /about", "Capabilities: laser cutting, CNC bending, welding (T