UPDATE companies SET description='Behlen Mfg. Co. was founded in 1936 in a garage in Columbus, Nebraska. What began as a small operation has grown into a multi-business manufacturer with locations spanning five states, including facilities in Columbus, Nebraska, and Sarasota, Florida. The company is led by a management team that includes Board Chair Tony Raimondo, Jr. and President & CEO Tom Boal.

The company produces a diverse line of metal products: metal building systems, livestock equipment, grain storage systems, strip joiners, and capacitor winding machines. Its Behlen Custom Fabrication unit supplies precision custom-fabricated metal components, while Behlen Joiner provides coil stitching for continuous line operations. Hilton Behlen Energy Systems builds precision winding machines for power and capacitor applications. BMC Transportation operates a dedicated flatbed fleet serving 48 states and Canadian provinces.

Behlen serves agricultural producers, commercial builders, energy companies, and transportation firms. Its Behlen Country line supports farmers and ranchers with gates, stock tanks, and farm equipment. Behlen Building Systems targets the metal construction market, and Behlen Grain Systems supplies grain bins and storage solutions. The energy division serves capacitor and power equipment manufacturers.

The company emphasizes a culture called PRIDE (Partners Responsible In Demonstrating Excellence), which empowers employees to halt processes that fall short of specifications. Its stated mission is to provide innovative solutions that drive customer success, empower employees, and strengthen communities. Behlen highlights over 85 years of manufacturing experience, a dedicated transportation network, and a commitment to sustainable practices using predominantly recycled steel.', certifications=ARRAY['IAS certificate','AISC certificate']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Custom metal fabrication", "Metal building systems manufacturing", "Grain storage systems manufacturing", "Livestock equipment manufacturing", "Strip joiner production", "Coil stitching", "Capacitor winding machine manufacturing", "Dedicated flatbed transportation", "Quality assurance (PRIDE system)", "Lean manufacturing (AIM program)", "Continuous improvement"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Metal building construction", "Grain storage", "Energy (capacitor and power equipment)", "Transportation and logistics", "Farm and ranch equipment"], "materials": ["Steel"], "equipment": ["Capacitor winding machines", "Strip joiners", "Coil stitching equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated flatbed fleet covering 48 states and Canadian provinces (BMC Transportation)", "PRIDE quality system empowering employees to stop non-conforming work", "Over 85 years of continuous manufacturing experience", "Integrated business units spanning agricultural, building, grain, energy, and transportation", "Sustainable manufacturing using predominantly recycled steel"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1936 in Columbus, Nebraska garage -> /about", "Multiple business units across five states -> /about", "Products: metal building systems, livestock equipment, grain storage, strip joiners, capacitor winding machines -> /", "Facilities in Columbus, NE and Sarasota, FL -> /", "Certifications: IAS certificate, AISC certificate -> /", "BMC Transportation dedicated fleet across 48 states and Canadian provinces -> /", "Quality system PRIDE (Partners Responsible In Demonstrating Excellence) -> /", "Leadership: Tony Raimondo, Jr. (Board Chair), Tom Boal (President & CEO) -> /about", "Mission, vision, purpose statements -> /about", "Sustainability: predominantly steel, most recycled material -> /about", "Over 85 years manufacturing experience -> /", "Behlen Country for farm/ranch equipment -> /", "Behlen Building Systems for metal buildings -> /", "Behlen Grain Systems for grain bins -> /", "Hilton Behlen Energy Systems for winding machines -> /", "Behlen Custom Fabrication for precision custom-fabricated metal components -> /", "Behlen Joiner for coil stitching -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our diverse line of products, from metal building systems to livestock equipment, grain storage systems, strip joiners, and capacitor winding machines, reflect our commitment to excellence and reliability.", "founded_year": "1936", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='behlen-mfg-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Belden traces its roots to 1902, when the Belden Manufacturing Company was incorporated in St. Louis, Missouri, with Joe Belden as president and Albert Beutler as plant superintendent. The firm began as a wire manufacturer and went public on the Midwest Stock Exchange in 1939 before joining Cooper Industries in 1980.

Today Belden produces cables and connectivity solutions for industrial and networking applications, including Ethernet and fiber‑optic cables designed for harsh environments. The company also delivers network design, installation, hypercare, and run‑and‑maintain services, supporting customers from initial assessment through ongoing operations. Global headcount is reported as 8 employees, with operations across 18 countries certified as Great Place to Work.

Belden serves industries such as consumer packaged goods, data centers, energy, hospitality, mass transit, and warehousing & logistics. In energy, it supplies hardened, IEC‑compliant connectivity for generation, transmission, and distribution; in mass transit, it provides industrial‑grade wired and wireless links for trains and trackside systems; in data centers, it offers end‑to‑end infrastructure from high‑density cabinets to cooling automation.

The company positions itself as a bridge between operational and information technology, emphasizing a unified “complete connection solutions” approach that integrates hardware, software, and services. Its early leadership in industrial Ethernet and fiber optics, plus a history of equipping everything from Apollo 11 to Olympic broadcasts, underpins its claim to turn connectivity challenges into competitive advantages.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable manufacturing", "Fiber optic cable manufacturing", "Ethernet cable manufacturing", "Connectivity solutions", "Network design services", "Network installation services", "Hypercare services", "Run & maintain services", "Network assessment services"], "industries": ["Consumer Packaged Goods", "Data Centers", "Energy", "Hospitality", "Mass Transit", "Warehousing & Logistics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First to market industrial Ethernet and fiber\u2011optic cables (early 1980s)", "Hardened, IEC\u2011compliant connectivity for energy grid applications", "End\u2011to\u2011end data\u2011center infrastructure including high\u2011density cabinets, fiber connectivity, and cooling automation", "Full\u2011lifecycle network services: design, install, hypercare, and run\u2011and\u2011maintain"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1902 as Belden Manufacturing Company -> /about-us", "Founders Joe Belden (president) and Albert Beutler (plant superintendent) -> /about-us", "Headquarters St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Went public on Midwest Stock Exchange 1939 -> /about-us", "Joined Cooper Industries 1980 -> /about-us", "First to market industrial Ethernet and fiber optic cables early 1980s -> /about-us", "Supplies hardened IEC-compliant connectivity for energy grid -> /", "Provides end-to-end data center infrastructure -> /", "Serves consumer packaged goods, data centers, energy, hospitality, mass transit, warehousing & logistics -> /", "Offers