UPDATE companies SET description='Benco Equipment, headquartered in Bismarck, North Dakota, has been serving automotive professionals and hobbyists since 1972. The company operates as a family-owned, six-location network across the Midwest and functions as a division of Automotive Parts Headquarters Inc. (APH), a third-generation family-owned aftermarket parts distributor founded in 1920 in Minneapolis as National Bushing & Parts Company.

Benco specializes in the sales, service, installation, inspection, and financing of automotive service equipment. Its six stores stock a large inventory of lifts, air compressors, tire equipment, A/C machines, diagnostic tools, piping systems, and waste oil heaters. Factory-trained technicians provide in-house and mobile repair services, manage replacement parts inventories, and perform inspections following ANSI/ALI ALOIM standards. The network also offers operator training and financing options.

The company serves automotive repair shops requiring light, medium, and heavy-duty lifts, as well as heavy-duty and industrial facilities, motorcycle and ATV shops, and hobbyists throughout the Midwest.

