UPDATE companies SET description='Bend Molding and Prototype operates from Bend, Oregon. The company was established by mechanical engineers for mechanical engineers, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. Leadership carries over 30 years of mechanical engineering experience, and the business positions itself as a domestic supplier focused on direct, machinist-level communication.

The shop specializes in fast-turn injection molding, taking plastic components from CAD designs through prototyping to full-scale production. All services—Design for Manufacturing (DFM), precision mold manufacturing, injection molding, and detailed quality reporting—are performed in-house. The engineering team also provides mechanical and product design, turning concepts into functional prototypes. Typical prototype lead time runs three to five weeks from DFM consultation to T1 samples.

The company serves mechanical engineers and product development teams needing plastic parts, though specific industry sectors are not listed. Customers gain a unified point of contact for the entire project lifecycle, from initial design through production.

Bend Molding and Prototype differentiates itself by offering the “talk to the machinist” experience, giving clients direct access to engineers and toolmakers. This collaborative approach aims to make the supplier an indispensable partner, navigating challenges with the same engineering perspective as its clients.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fast-turn injection molding", "Prototyping", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "Precision mold manufacturing", "Quality reporting", "Mechanical design", "Product design", "Prototype design"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production", "lead_time": "3\u20135 weeks from DFM consultation to T1 samples", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct access to engineers and toolmakers", "In-house DFM, mold manufacturing, injection molding, and quality reporting", "Prototype components in 3\u20135 weeks from DFM to T1 samples", "Established by mechanical engineers for mechanical engineers", "Unified point of contact from CAD to production"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bend, Oregon -> /about", "Established by mechanical engineers for mechanical engineers -> /", "Over 30 years of mechanical engineering experience -> /", "Specializes in fast-turn injection molding -> /about, /services", "In-house DFM, mold manufacturing, injection molding, quality reporting -> /services", "Prototype lead time 3-5 weeks from DFM to T1 samples -> /services", "Mechanical and product design services -> /services", "Direct access to engineers and toolmakers -> /about", "Unified point of contact from CAD to production -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "comprehensive services are entirely available in-house. This includes Design For Manufacturing (DFM), precision mold manufacturing, injection molding, and detailed quality reporting", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bend-molding-and-prototype' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Benfield Control Systems Inc., operating as Benfield Electric Supply Co. Inc., is headquartered in Mount Vernon, New York, with a second location in White Plains. The company was founded in 1951 and remains independently owned, having grown from a local electrical supply house into a multi-division distributor serving the New York metropolitan area and beyond.

The business operates across six divisions: Benfield Electric Supply, Benfield Data Comm, Benfield Electric & Elevator Supply, Benfield Control Systems, Lighting, and International. Its 24 service trucks support same-day pickup and next-day delivery across New York City and the Lower Hudson Valley. The company maintains a broad inventory of electrical distribution equipment, elevator wire and rope, building wire, fire alarm cable, conduit, cable tray, lighting, motor control centers, switchboards, panelboards, medium-voltage switchgear up to 38 kV, UPS systems, VFDs, and UL 508A-listed industrial control panels. In-house capabilities include value engineering, project management, RCDD-certified data engineers, FOA-certified fiber optic technicians, pre-fabrication, SCADA/CPMS software development, and custom power distribution system design.

Benfield serves industrial enterprises, corporations, original equipment manufacturers, and construction firms. Other markets include commercial construction, data communications, elevator systems, HVAC, power distribution, and renewable energy such as solar, wind, and EV charging infrastructure.

