UPDATE companies SET description='Benteler Automotive Corporation traces its roots to 1876 when Carl Benteler opened a small hardware store in Bielefeld, Germany. The company evolved from trading into a global metal-processing and automotive technology group. Its U.S. headquarters are in Goshen, Indiana, while the global holding is based in Salzburg, Austria.

Today Benteler operates as a metal-processing specialist with more than 20,000 employees across roughly 90 sites in 25 countries. Its manufacturing footprint includes stamping, assembly, module and chassis production, as well as seamless and welded tube mills and steelmaking facilities. The company also runs tool shops, machinery manufacturing units, engineering hubs, and shared-service centers in Europe and the Americas.

The business serves primarily the automotive industry as a Tier 1 supplier of chassis components, module assemblies, and structural parts. It also supplies precision steel tubes to energy providers and industrial customers for applications requiring high load capacity and durability. Concrete examples from its portfolio include crash management systems, axle modules, and free-cutting steel tubing for hydraulic and mechanical uses.

Benteler emphasizes its 150-year heritage of "pioneering spirit in motion" and a focus on making mobility safer and more sustainable. The company says its differentiation lies in combining deep material expertise with full-process control—from steelmaking to finished modules—to deliver integrated, lightweight solutions for OEMs worldwide.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Stamping", "Assembly", "Module assembly", "Chassis component manufacturing", "Seamless tube production", "Welded tube production", "Steel production", "Tool making", "Machinery manufacturing", "Engineering services", "Shared business services"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Energy", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Steel", "Free cutting steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["150 years of pioneering spirit since 1876", "Global Tier 1 supplier with ~90 locations in 25 countries", "Full-process metal expertise: steelmaking, tube production, stamping, and module assembly", "Over 20,000 employees worldwide", "Focus on safer, more sustainable mobility"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1876 by Carl Benteler in Bielefeld -> /about-us", "U.S. headquarters in Goshen, Indiana -> db", "More than 20,000 employees -> /about-us", "Around 90 locations in 25 countries -> /about-us", "Global Tier 1 supplier -> /about-us", "Metal processing specialists: stamping, assembly, tube and steel production -> /, /about-us", "Industries: Automotive, Energy, Industrial -> industries_served, /", "Materials: Steel, Free cutting steel -> /", "Capabilities: Stamping, Assembly, Module assembly, Chassis components, Seamless tube production, Welded tube production, Steel production, Tool making, Machinery manufacturing, Engineering services, Shared business services -> /, products array"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a global tier 1 supplier in all relevant markets with around 90 locations in 25 countries, we are always at our customer''s side.", "founded_year": "1876", "employee_count": "20,000+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='benteler-automotive-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Benton & Sons Fabrication operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in Pikeville, North Carolina, about 60 miles southeast of Raleigh. The company was founded in 1983 by Ben Benton Jr. and remains family-owned and operated, with three generations of the Benton family having worked in the business.

The shop specializes in heavy steel plate fabrication, stainless steel sheet metal fabrication, and the customized assembly of machinery and equipment. Core processes include plate rolling, brake press forming, punching, shearing, laser cutting, and water jet cutting. Notable equipment includes a 1,000-ton by 24-foot CNC-controlled Cincinnati brake press, a TRUMPF 6,000-watt TruLaser 5060, and a Mitsubishi 6030XL laser cutter—one of only two in the Western Hemisphere. The facility features multiple bays, large overhead doors, and overhead cranes to handle large-scale fabrications and assemblies such as structural steel components, machine bases, commercial kitchen equipment, pharmaceutical and laboratory apparatus, and decorative metal yard art.

Benton & Sons serves customers across the Southeast and Mid-Atlantic, including Maryland, Virginia, the Carolinas, and Georgia. Its client base spans food processing, commercial kitchens, pharmaceutical plants, shipbuilding, nuclear facilities, transportation, beverage bottling, and fine chemicals. The company’s proximity to I-95, I-40, rail lines, and East Coast ports supports domestic and international shipping.

