UPDATE companies SET description='Berle Manufacturing Co. has operated from Charleston, South Carolina since its founding in 1951. The company remains in the hands of the founding family, making it the oldest family-owned trouser manufacturer in the United States still under the same ownership. Over seven decades later, the business continues to design and produce men''s trousers, khakis, and shorts from its Charleston base.

The product line spans dress pants, casual khakis, and shorts crafted from premium fabrics including cotton, linen, wool, polyester, corduroy, and seersucker. Signature construction details feature brass zippers, watch pockets, Italian waistbands, true two-piece French flies, and corozo buttons. The company offers multiple fit profiles — slim, classic, relaxed — and rise options (regular, short, long) across brands such as Berle, Vintage 1946, Charleston Khakis, and Self Sizer.

Berle serves the men''s apparel market primarily through direct-to-consumer channels, shipping to customers across the United States. Its assortment targets professionals and enthusiasts seeking tailored trousers for work, social occasions, and leisure, with a noted emphasis on patterned and fancy styles that the company describes as one of the industry''s largest selections.

