UPDATE companies SET description='Blue-Top Steering Gears operates from Stanton, North Dakota. In 2011, Ryan, son of the previous owner Myron, purchased the business and re-established it in Stanton. Ryan brought experience from re-manufacturing steering gears with a large company in Seattle, Washington.

All machining and assembly work is kept in-house, with the facility equipped for complete remanufacturing. The company also offers a rebuild-and-return service for customers'' own OEM cores.

Its catalog includes dozens of part numbers tailored to specific model years and configurations, such as 32-spline and 36-spline output shafts for Ford trucks and various master-spline arrangements for GM and Dodge axles.

